{
  "format": "souls-form-cases/1",
  "about": "eden:pruning_shrub (from #1748). Six named soft shoots, each a bool that starts true, and a count of the cuttings kept in the shrub's own tray. Anyone with a free hand prunes one chosen shoot (one form, `prune`, whose `shoot` argument is one of the six shoot fields the form lists): walks to the stand, pinches at that shoot's tip for four seconds, the shoot is gone for good and one more cutting lies in the tray. Refused, as the original refused: a shoot already pruned ('That shoot has already been pruned; it cannot regrow.') and no free hand ('Put down what you hold before hand pruning.'). No form sets a shoot back to true, so a pruned shoot names no fix. A shoot outside the form's own list (here `cuttings`, a field of the shrub the form does not name) is bad input, so the form never writes a field it does not name.",
